---
/**
 * ASSESSMENT & SUPPORT · HOMEWORK POLICY — audit 2.D2.
 *
 * ⚠ THE SCHOOL PUBLISHES ONE SENTENCE ABOUT HOMEWORK. Homework rules govern a
 * family's evenings, so a plausible-sounding invention here would be among the
 * most damaging things this site could print. The page carries that sentence,
 * says plainly that the rest is not published, and does not describe a policy.
 *
 * ⚠ BUT IT IS NO LONGER A ONE-LINE PAGE, because a second, better piece of
 * evidence turned up in the school's own photography rather than its text: the
 * Parents' Forum agenda, projected and legible, puts homework on the record as a
 * standing item parents may raise. Read off the school's photograph:
 *
 *   "Agenda for Parents Forum: Session 2025-26, Class IX to XII"
 *     5)  Quality of assignment in Learner's Comate / Class work / Homework
 *     11) Correction of Notebooks / Learner's Comate
 *
 * That is worth more to a parent than a paragraph of homework philosophy: it is
 * the channel through which the homework question is actually answered.
 *
 * ⚠ "LEARNER'S COMATE" IS TRANSCRIBED, NOT INTERPRETED. It is the school's own
 * spelling on its own slide, and it is quoted rather than expanded, because what
 * the artefact is — a diary, a workbook, a portfolio — is not published.
 *
 * ⚠ NOT CLAIMED: minutes per night, days per subject, a weekend rule, a holiday
 * rule, or a policy document. None is published.
 *
 * Composition: statement (sand) → split (paper, photo LEFT — the forum) → close.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import AcStatement from '../../../components/academics/system/AcStatement.astro';
import AcSplit from '../../../components/academics/system/AcSplit.astro';
import AcClose from '../../../components/academics/system/AcClose.astro';

import banner from '../../../assets/photos/sb-library.jpg';
import pPanel from '../../../assets/parents forum/parents forum (5).jpg';
import pSeated from '../../../assets/parents forum/parents forum (2).jpg';
import pCohort from '../../../assets/photos/sunbeem-3.jpg';

const school = 'Sunbeam School Ballia';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Homework Policy — Sunbeam School Ballia"
  description="What Sunbeam School Ballia publishes about homework: that it is set to a published pattern, and that the quality of assignments and the correction of notebooks are standing items on the Parents' Forum agenda."
>
  <PageHero
    title="Homework Policy"
    standfirst="One published sentence, one published agenda item — and nothing invented to fill the gap between them."
    crumbs={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Academics', href: '/academics/' },
      { label: 'Assessment & Support', href: '/academics/assessment/' },
    ]}
    src={banner}
    alt="Students of Sunbeam School Ballia reading at the long tables of the library, a member of staff at the head of the row."
    position="50% 46%"
  />

  <div class="u-page-panel ac-panel">
    <AcStatement
      ground="sand"
      ghost="Prep"
      ghostAt="left"
      texture={true}
      kicker="What the school publishes"
      statement="A pattern,<br /><em>not a policy.</em>"
      body={[
        'The school states one thing about homework: that it is <strong>set to a published pattern</strong> rather than assigned subject by subject on the day. That is the whole of it.',
        'So the whole of it is what appears here. No minutes per night, no days per subject, no weekend rule, no holiday rule — because none of those is published, and a family that plans its evenings around an invented figure would be planning around us rather than around the school.',
      ]}
    />

    <AcSplit
      ground="paper"
      side="left"
      aspect="3 / 2"
      kicker="Where the question is actually answered"
      heading="Item five,<br /><em>and item eleven</em>"
      body={[
        'The more useful fact is not on the school’s homework page at all — it is projected on a screen in its Parents’ Forum. The agenda for the <strong>2025-26 forum for Classes IX to XII</strong> runs to twelve items, and two of them are this subject: <em>“quality of assignment in Learner’s Comate / class work / homework”</em>, and <em>“correction of notebooks / Learner’s Comate.”</em>',
        'A parent who wants to know how much homework is set, and whether it comes back marked, has a standing item on a published agenda to raise it under. That is a better answer than a paragraph describing a policy this site cannot verify.',
      ]}
      photo={pPanel}
      alt={`The leadership panel at a Parents’ Forum session at ${school}, the session’s twelve-item agenda projected on the screen beside them`}
      inset={pSeated}
      insetAlt={`Parents of ${school} seated in the tiered rows of the hall during a Parents’ Forum session`}
    />

    <AcClose
      owed={true}
      statement="Set to a pattern.<br /><em>The pattern is owed.</em>"
      body="The school publishes that homework follows a pattern and gives parents a forum item to raise it under. The pattern itself — the load, the days, the weekend and holiday rules — is not published anywhere on its site."
      photo={pCohort}
      alt={`Students and staff of ${school} gathered on the hall stage`}
      position="50% 42%"
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ac-panel { padding-block: 0; }
</style>
